#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55723dcb-605f-595d-8fae-1ee5436e7a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384648} {:answer/id #uuid "42a8ae72-16c3-587a-a3e7-b75bffe928ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-5y+z-70=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384649} {:answer/id #uuid "803a1755-2134-5aa8-a86a-8015bacc22d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+y-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384650} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd5cb89-4f60-5887-afe3-a7c5a3523298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z+70=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384651} {:answer/id #uuid "31dcdae4-9b1f-53d5-a9d2-7fbe89fc944a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2y+3z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55723dcb-605f-595d-8fae-1ee5436e7a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384648} :answer-field/id #uuid "362de8bd-fdfa-5aa6-b00e-5111d888298e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5938084-81eb-59aa-b8c4-275f8497be94" :question/math-academy-id "q-33142" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(2,-5,1)$, $P(4,-2,3)$ and $Q(5,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨2,-5,1⟩,\\,p=⟨4,-2,3⟩,$ and $q=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,3⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,2⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨5,1,0⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-15i+8j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-15,8,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z+67 & =0 \\\\ 15x-8y-3z-67 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Plane Given Its Cartesian Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0eb7ad-9b50-5dc6-8b87-7f76312128ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0eb7ad-9b50-5dc6-8b87-7f76312128ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384670} :answer-field/id #uuid "b27f8f14-201a-514c-be9b-ed56526f88d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e32d4500-7940-5053-86bb-fbf9704e32fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e32d4500-7940-5053-86bb-fbf9704e32fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384672} :answer-field/id #uuid "40f9f4ed-dcee-5879-891b-4aeea776472c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8a3a99-7496-5337-b5d9-580ecd2bdac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c8a3a99-7496-5337-b5d9-580ecd2bdac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384674} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ce9af2-3886-50d4-8ccd-8959a18d4900" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e72d0f67-c2b4-5692-91cc-01e26d063987" :question/math-academy-id "q-336228" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $5x+2y+z-4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨$\n{{field-2}} $,\\,2\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨5,2,1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y+z-4 & =0 \\\\ z & =-5x-2y+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,\\,2\\,,1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
